# =============================================================================
# Lead Capture Pro — backup VPS authorized_keys (EXAMPLE, B23 G-6D C1)
# =============================================================================
# Two separate local accounts on the BACKUP VPS, each with exactly ONE key and
# exactly ONE forced command. `restrict` disables PTY allocation, agent, X11
# and TCP forwarding and user rc files; the client's requested command is
# handed to the forced command in SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND and parsed as the
# two-verb LCP-OFFHOST/1 protocol — a shell is never reachable.
#
# Public keys only ever appear here. Private keys: the upload key lives in the
# primary VPS deploy user's ~/.ssh (mode 600); the audit key lives in the
# primary deploy user's ~/.ssh AND as a GitHub Actions secret; neither is
# committed anywhere. Replace the <…> placeholders during activation.
#
# /home/lcp-receive/.ssh/authorized_keys   (owner lcp-receive, mode 600)
restrict,command="/opt/lcp-offhost/bin/offhost-receive.sh" ssh-ed25519 <UPLOAD-PUBLIC-KEY-BASE64> lcp-offhost-upload@primary

# /home/lcp-audit/.ssh/authorized_keys     (owner lcp-audit, mode 600)
restrict,command="/opt/lcp-offhost/bin/offhost-audit.sh" ssh-ed25519 <AUDIT-PUBLIC-KEY-BASE64> lcp-offhost-audit

# sshd_config on the backup VPS (activation prerequisite):
#   PasswordAuthentication no
#   PubkeyAuthentication yes
#   PermitRootLogin no
#   AllowUsers lcp-receive lcp-audit <operator-account>
# The vault identity (lcp-vault) and the publisher have NO SSH login at all.
